From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 08:30:22 -0400
Subject: float a Space's name above its chip on hover

The reference raises a small pill with the Space's name when a chip is hovered.
An earlier attempt reserved a row for the name and moved the icons the moment
it appeared, which put the hovered chip out from under the pointer; this one is
an overlay. The chip reports hover with its bounds, and the region view
positions a layout-ignored label pill centred above it, clamped to the sidebar.

Verified with synthetic mouse moves posted to the browser's own process: the
pill reads "Space 2" above the second chip and nothing else moves.

Why: the name pill is how the reference tells Spaces apart without labels.
Removable when: never, short of dropping Spaces.
